objective:
Four checks, all on the shared CartesianGrid:
(1) FV diffusion of cos(πx/L)cos(πy/L) (21×21, L = 10 µm, D = 1, dt = 0.01, t = 1 s)
    against exp(-2π²Dt/L²);
(2) 20,000 particles diffusing from the centre cell (D = 1, 4 seeds): the variance of the
    binned positions, minus dx²/6 (the initial cell spread plus Sheppard's binning
    correction), against 2Dt;
(3) the histogram sum equals the molecule count at every record;
(4) 100,000 uniform particles after 2 s of diffusion (11×11, 4 seeds): the counts per
    node class (corner, edge, interior) match their element-volume shares.

conclusion:
All four checks pass (results/metrics.json, 2026-10-03; re-run after the record-time fix):
- FV vs analytic: 6.0e-4 relative error;
- binned particle variance vs 2Dt: 0.13% (0.96% before the fix, which was the one-step record lag);
- histogram mismatch: 0 molecules;
- node classes vs volume shares: max |z| = 0.48. Corner and edge concentrations are
  within 0.4% of interior.
Both halves and the handoff behave as specified.
